              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tara Heaney"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipee. I boiled it longer to make sure it set and for fun I added a peeled, diced apple.",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-11T23:10:42.420Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shasta"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So this review is a little late because I have been making this recipe every holiday since I first found it about six years ago. It's been a big hit at every holiday gathering. I never really liked cranberry sauce before but I was asked to bring some to a family gathering, found this recipe and it is so good. I let the cranberries cook a little longer and I find it helps it to thicken a bit more. Let it set in the fridge over night and the consistency is perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-08T02:57:17.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katzmagick in the Kitchen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "There are a few small issues I had with this recipe. It does not tell you how to use the ginger and cinnamon stick. I chopped the ginger in small pieces and took the cinnamon stick out before putting into a dish. I added a little bit of orange zest. The sauce at first seems very sweet, but the orange leaves a good after note. overall, sauce came out good.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-24T16:29:45.677Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sbb16"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is delicious. Like the other reviewers mentioned, it needs to be boiled till it thickens up, but once it does, it's truly delicious. I used a few dashes of grated cinnamon instead of a cinnamon stick and added a splash or orange juice.",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-28T14:09:22.323Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lauren Brunswick"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love it! I added a bit of orange extract to give it a kick(as i have no oranges in the house) and it turned out wonderfully! The only thing is that i'd say it needs to cook more than 5 minutes - i think it took me almost 10 - to get a good consistency. That might just be my preference, though.",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-21T22:17:52.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "R_McMullen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very easy. It was not too strong. Everybody loved it. Just remember to boil it long enought for it to be thick.",
